## Legal text

### Article 41 – Penalties

1\. The Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties applicable to infringements of [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen) and of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex II that impose obligations on economic operators and shall take all measures necessary to ensure that they are implemented in accordance with national law.

2\. The penalties provided for shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive.

3\. The Member States shall, by 16 October 2021, notify those provisions to the Commission, where they have not previously been notified, and shall notify it, without delay, of any subsequent amendment affecting them.

### Article 42 – Evaluation, review and guidelines

1\. By 31 December 2026 and every five years thereafter, the Commission shall carry out an evaluation of [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen) in light of the objectives that it pursues and shall present a report thereon to the European Parliament, to the Council and to the European Economic and Social Committee.

2\. The report shall assess whether [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen) achieved its objective, in particular with regard to reducing the number of non-compliant products on the Union market, ensuring effective and efficient enforcement of Union harmonisation legislation within the Union, improving cooperation between competent authorities and strengthening the controls on products entering the Union market, while taking into account the impact on business and in particular on SMEs. In addition, the evaluation shall also assess the scope of [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen), the effectiveness of the peer review system and of the market surveillance activities that receive Union financing in the light of the requirements of Union policies and law and the possibilities to further improve the cooperation between the market surveillance authorities and customs authorities.

3\. By 16 July 2023, the Commission shall prepare an evaluation report on the implementation of Article [4](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-2#article-4-tasks-of-economic-operators-regarding-products-subject-to-certain-union-harmonisation-legislation). The report shall in particular evaluate the scope of that Article, its effects and its costs and benefits. The report shall be accompanied, where appropriate, by a legislative proposal.

4\. Within four years after the first approval of a specific system of product-related pre-export control referred to in Article [35](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-35-international-cooperation)(3), the Commission shall carry out an evaluation of its effects and cost efficiency.

5\. In order to facilitate the implementation of [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen), the Commission shall draw up guidelines for the practical implementation of Article [4](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-2#article-4-tasks-of-economic-operators-regarding-products-subject-to-certain-union-harmonisation-legislation) for the purposes of market surveillance authorities and economic operators.

### Article 43 – Committee procedure

1\. The Commission shall be assisted by a committee. That committee shall be a committee within the meaning of [Regulation (EU) No 182/2011](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011R0182).

2\. Where reference is made to this paragraph, Article [5](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011R0182) of [Regulation (EU) No 182/2011](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011R0182) shall apply.

Where the committee delivers no opinion, the Commission shall not adopt the draft implementing act in respect of the implementing powers referred to in Article [11](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-4#article-11-activities-of-market-surveillance-authorities)(4), Article [21](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-5#article-21-union-testing-facilities)(9), Article [25](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-7#article-25-controls-on-products-entering-the-union-market)(8), Article [35](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-35-international-cooperation)(10) and Article [35](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-35-international-cooperation)(11) of [this Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen), and the third subparagraph of Article [5](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-2#article-5-authorised-representative)(4) of [Regulation (EU) No 182/2011](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32011R0182) shall apply.

### Article 44 – Entry into force and application

[This Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen) shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.

It shall apply from 16 July 2021. However, Articles [29](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-29-union-product-compliance-network), [30](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-30-composition-and-functioning-of-the-network), [31](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-31-role-and-tasks-of-the-network), [32](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-32-role-and-tasks-of-administrative-cooperation-groups), [33](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-8#article-33-role-and-tasks-of-the-commission) and [36](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen/kap-9#article-36-financing-activities) shall apply from 1 January 2021.

[This Regulation](/lagstiftning/marknadskontrollforordningen) shall be binding in its entirety and directly applicable in all Member States.

#### Signature

Done at Brussels, 20 June 2019.

For the European Parliament

The President

A. TAJANI

For the Council

The President

G. CIAMBA

